WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.961
A model router selects an endpoint using task type, data sensitivity, model capability,

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:06.830
latency target, availability, and cost.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.943
The eligible set should be determined by policy before performance ranking.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:15.430
A cloud model that would answer best is not eligible if the

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.674
prompt contains data that cannot leave.

00:00:17.674 --> 00:00:21.787
Record the route and policy result so behavior can be explained.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:27.021
Local servers and cloud endpoints may expose similar APIs, but details differ across streaming,

00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:30.760
tool calls, context limits, embeddings, error codes, and safety behavior.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.873
Normalize only the features the application uses and test each route.

00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:39.360
Model outputs are not interchangeable, so fallback may change quality or format.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.351
Clients need clear expectations when service is degraded.

00:00:42.351 --> 00:00:44.221
Apply rate limits, timeouts, queues,

00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:47.960
and concurrency controls separately for local capacity and paid endpoints.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.447
A local queue should not silently overflow into an expensive cloud route

00:00:52.447 --> 00:00:54.690
without a cost and privacy decision.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.429
Fallback logic must distinguish capacity failure, authentication failure, policy denial,

00:00:58.429 --> 00:00:59.551
and provider outage.

00:00:59.551 --> 00:01:03.290
Some failures should stop the request instead of rerouting it.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:08.151
Protect endpoint credentials and keep them out of prompts, client code, and logs.

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:13.012
Avoid orchestration that copies entire conversations to every candidate model before selecting one.

00:01:13.012 --> 00:01:17.125
Start with explicit routing rules and a small number of endpoints.

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:20.864
Add automation only when monitoring shows a recurring placement need.

00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:23.107
Good orchestration makes data movement, cost,

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:27.220
and failure visible rather than hiding complexity behind one chat box.
